.TH TRUNC 1.SH NAMEtrunc \- cut a file to a length.SH SYNOPSIS\fBtrunc\fRpath length.SH DESCRIPTION\fBtrunc\fRsets the length of the file\fIpath\fRto\fIlength\fRbytes, dropping everything after that.  The length is decimal, orhexadecimal after\fB$\fRor\fB0x\fR:\fR\fBtrunc notes 4\fRand\fBtrunc notes 0x4\fRboth keep the first four bytes.  By Carsten Emde, for non-commercialuse..SH SEE ALSOcombine, split